PS5 display: HDMI chip fixes, CEC, VRR, 4K120 and USB-C DisplayPort

- PS5 HDMI: ps5-linux-patches #49, #50 and #54, ported from 7.2 to 7.3
- PS5 HDMI: re-arm the output after the same display re-announces itself
- PS5 HDMI output fixes
- PS5 HDMI resolutions
- PS5 HDMI: debug log of bridge notifications and picture setups
- PS5 HDMI: full-rate DP link to the HDMI bridge
- PS5 HDMI: CEC (ps5-linux-patches #53 by Slip), ported to 7.3
- PS5 HDMI: mute and leave HDR when the output goes down
- PS5 HDMI: SCDC Source Version at every video setup
- PS5: USB-C DisplayPort output (PSVR2) and GFX1013 fixes, ported to 7.3
- PS5 HDMI: full RGB range in the AVI InfoFrame (hdmi.rgb_range)
- PS5 HDMI: EDID fallback when no connector is bound
- PS5 HDMI: keep the previous EDID on a short or invalid announcement
- PS5 HDMI (Verde): IT content and content type "game" in the AVI InfoFrame
- PS5 HDMI: no hang on the blinking cursor when switching sessions
- PS5 HDMI: RGB range flag encoded correctly (CTA-861 Q1:Q0)
- PS5 USB-C DP: off by default, opt in with usbc_dp.enable=1
- PS5 VRR on FLAVA3 consoles, switched with Steam's VRR setting
- PS5 VRR: stock PHY tail and VSync block in every setup again
- PS5 HDMI: 4K120 over HDMI 2.1 FRL on FLAVA3 (Lawson), hdmi.frl_4k120
- PS5 VRR: a running follow block stops when a newer setup starts
- PS5 VRR: never below 48 Hz, FreeSync SPD with the actual range
- PS5 HDMI: 4K120 only where it can work, and back to 4K60 by itself when it doesn't
- PS5 VRR: only for displays with HDMI VRR, as on the PS5 system
- PS5 HDMI: SCDC TMDS_Config at every setup for SCDC sinks, as a PC does
- PS5 VRR: HDMI VRR with an open-ended VRRmax, and the HF-SCDB
